<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lunavada</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lunavada is a town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the Mahi river, and the headquarters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahisagar-district">Mahisagar district</a>. Founded according to tradition in 1434, it was the capital of the princely state of Lunavada, ruled by a Solanki Rajput dynasty, until the state merged into independent India in 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lunavada.jpg" alt="Lunavada" width="320" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maywe46 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahisagar_District%27s_Court.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
